{; The cluster handle one proc carries: everything a turn needs and
 ; nothing it does not. The EVALUATOR IS INJECTED as a qualified symbol
 ; (the same symbols-as-data idiom as :seon.ancestor/populate), so the
 ; loop's mechanics do not wait on the seon.sci.eval adoption and a
 ; suite can drive a turn with a fake evaluator.
 ; `:seon.cluster.loop/stream-channel` is the cluster's ONE stream conn
 ; (F2 §2.1): a `(sliding-buffer 1)` in-port of the render proc onto
 ; which the `:call` arm's sink offers complete `:seon.ai/partial`
 ; snapshots. OPTIONAL because a suite or a REPL drives a turn without a
 ; render pipeline — absent means the call runs one-shot.
 :seon.cluster.loop/cluster [:map {:closed true} [:seon.store/branch-connection :seon.store/branch-connection] [:seon.cluster.run/process :seon.cluster.run/process] [:seon.cluster.wake/channel :seon.flow/channel] [:seon.cluster.loop/stream-channel {:optional true} :seon.flow/channel] [:seon.cluster.loop/completion :seon.flow/channel] [:seon.ai/primary :seon.ai/target] [:seon.ai/backup {:optional true} :seon.ai/target] [:seon.ai.retry/strategy :seon.ai.retry/strategy] [:seon.cluster.loop/evaluate :qualified-symbol] [:seon.sci.admit/caps :seon.sci.admit/caps] [:seon.config.eval/time-limit-ms :seon.config.eval/time-limit-ms] [:seon.config/on-core-error :seon.config/on-core-error] [:seon.config.error/recurrence-limit :seon.config.error/recurrence-limit] [:seon.config.message/max-chain :seon.config.message/max-chain] [:seon.config.error/escalate-to {:optional true} :seon.config.error/escalate-to] [:clojure.core.async.flow/pid {:optional true} :keyword]]
 ; `::flow/pid` is FLOW'S, added to the args map it hands the init
 ; arity (`flow/impl.clj:155`: `:args (assoc args ::flow/pid pid)`), so
 ; the handle a running proc holds genuinely has one and the closed
 ; shape has to say so. Optional because a suite or a REPL builds the
 ; handle itself and flow adds the key only at start. Instrumentation
 ; found this the first time it ran against a real boot — the contract
 ; was wrong about its own live input and nothing had ever checked.
 ; `:seon.cluster.loop/provider` is DELETED, not deprecated. It was this
 ; exact four-key map under a second name, and once `seon.ai/targets`
 ; derives both roles from the dials there is nothing for a loop-local
 ; copy of the shape to be. The handle now carries `:seon.ai/primary`
 ; and the OPTIONAL `:seon.ai/backup` — `targets`' own keys, merged in
 ; whole, so the handle cannot re-key them wrongly.
 ; `:seon.cluster.eval/output` is what the form PRINTED, captured as
 ; bounded receipt evidence. Both closed shapes below omitted it while
 ; the code has threaded it since the base-ctx fixes — a contract wrong
 ; about its own live input, exactly the class instrumentation found
 ; four of at step 4. Review-caught 2026-07-27.
 :seon.cluster.loop/evaluation [:map {:closed true} [:seon.sci.admit/value :any] [:seon.cluster.eval/result-edn {:optional true} :seon.cluster.eval/result-edn] [:seon.cluster.eval/error {:optional true} :seon.cluster.eval/error] [:seon.cluster.eval/interrupted-at {:optional true} :seon.cluster.eval/interrupted-at] [:seon.cluster.eval/output {:optional true} :seon.cluster.eval/output] [:seon.cluster.eval/ns {:optional true} :seon.cluster.eval/ns] [:seon.sci.eval/program-row {:optional true} :seon.sci.eval/program-row]]
 :seon.cluster.loop/turn-request [:map {:closed true} [:seon.cluster.loop/cluster :seon.cluster.loop/cluster] [:seon.cluster.work/next :seon.cluster.work/next]]
 :seon.cluster.loop/terminal-request [:map {:closed true} [:seon.cluster.run/id :seon.cluster.run/id] [:seon.cluster.run/process :seon.cluster.run/process] [:seon.cluster.run.form/ordinal :seon.cluster.run.form/ordinal] [:seon.cluster.eval/result-edn {:optional true} :seon.cluster.eval/result-edn] [:seon.cluster.eval/error {:optional true} :seon.cluster.eval/error] [:seon.cluster.eval/interrupted-at {:optional true} :seon.cluster.eval/interrupted-at] [:seon.error/kind {:optional true} :seon.error/kind] [:seon.cluster.eval/output {:optional true} :seon.cluster.eval/output] [:seon.cluster.eval/ns {:optional true} :seon.cluster.eval/ns] [:seon.sci.eval/program-row {:optional true} :seon.sci.eval/program-row] [:my.run/value {:optional true} :my.run/value]]
 ; The central pass's own proc state and turn counter died with it
 ; (F2 §3.1); the surviving turn proc keeps its state keys in agent.edn.
 :seon.cluster.loop/completion :seon.flow/channel

 ; One completed turn, for observation only. The run id is OPTIONAL
 ; because an `:open` turn reports before a run exists — the report is
 ; built by a `cond->` that omits it, and the closed shape said
 ; required, so the contract had been wrong about its own most common
 ; report since it was written (instrumentation found it) — the loop's out port
 ; carries a report nothing depends on, so a dropped report costs
 ; nothing and no consumer can backpressure the loop.
 :seon.cluster.loop/turn-report [:map {:closed true} [:seon.cluster.run/id {:optional true} :seon.cluster.run/id] [:seon.cluster.agent/id :seon.cluster.agent/id] [:seon.cluster.work/situation :seon.cluster.work/situation] [:seon.cluster.loop/forms-run [:int {:min 0}]] [:seon.cluster.loop/outcome [:enum :closed :released :error :interrupted]]]
 :seon.cluster.loop/forms-run [:int {:min 0}]
 :seon.cluster.loop/outcome [:enum :closed :released :error :interrupted]}
